From bd5de183c3dd9848b0e4e7d016d87724c387d6e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:38:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3: remove accidental sunday_chill lock, enforce library
 purity, fix garage focus/social contradiction

Fix 1: resolveVagueWorldCommit no longer default-commits sunday_chill_world for
unmatched low-confidence prompts (now passthrough), so inferWorldIdentityIdsFromPrompt
/ resolveWorldBoundary no longer hard-lock them. "hospital waiting" removed from
the sunday_chill everyday patterns. Genuine everyday/named worlds unchanged.

Fix 2: new lib/library-delivery-guard.ts; the /generate handler filters
deliveredTracks and finalApiTracks to verified Liked Songs ids in library mode
immediately before Spotify / saved-playlist / cache side effects. Discovery
mode (noLibraryMode) untouched. Empty result -> LIBRARY_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_PROMPT.

Fix 3: garage hangout prompts no longer resolve to activity "focus" in
core/v3/intent.ts; isGarageHangoutContext is shared with the controller's
upbeat-social gate so the two cannot disagree.

Tests: regression tests in vague-world-commit, activity-profiles and new
library-delivery-guard suites; one v6 assertion that depended on the removed
default lock updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
